From 831044df8ca737144987d6593a87cee31350b73c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:48:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: texture writes reach only the cached pages they change:
 same bytes skipped, exact rectangles, pages updated in place

- t30 at 864x488 ran 50-60 fps most of the time, with stretches of 16-30 fps: 150-220 pages
  decoded a second, ~27000 misses and as many invalidations in a session. Every write to the
  texture store freed each cached page it reached, by 16x16 cells at the next Prepare: a palette
  row took every page using any CLUT in those 16 rows, a small image every page (all its CLUTs)
  at that place, whether or not the bytes had changed.
- TextureStore::Upload compares first: the bytes already there change nothing
  (THPS_GL_SAMEBYTES=0: written anyway).
- The cache is told the exact rectangle right after the write (GlGpu::TexturesWritten;
  THPS_GL_PRECISEINV=0: the cells at the next Prepare).
- Texels written to a page drawn in the last 4 frames: the rows touched (8-row bands) are decoded
  again in its slot, which stays valid (THPS_GL_PARTIAL=0: freed). A CLUT, a texture window, a
  page wrapping at VRAM's edge, a write of 64 rows or more, or a page not drawn lately: freed as
  before. The per-frame check against the store (CacheCheck, "stale") still watches for misses.
- [gl] line: texture writes skipped as the same bytes, pages updated in place, freed. Boot line
  "[gl] texture cache writes: ...".
---
 platform/pc/README.md           |  3 ++
 platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h |  8 ++++
 platform/pc/src/pc_gpu_gl.cpp   | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 platform/pc/src/pc_texstore.cpp | 23 ++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/pc/README.md b/platform/pc/README.md
index 633142a..0bbb987 100644
--- a/platform/pc/README.md
+++ b/platform/pc/README.md
@@ -576,6 +576,9 @@ window, `THPS_FAST`, `THPS_DETERMINISTIC`) never wait for a display.
 | `THPS_GL_GPUTIME=1` | Vita, a measurement: each frame drawn to the end before the swap, the GPU time logged (`[gpu]`); slower |
 | `THPS_GL_HALF=0` | OpenGL ES (Vita): the opaque no-discard program's colour maths in full precision (default t30: half, where the compiler takes it) |
 | `THPS_DATA_BUCKETS=0` | Vita: Data's files stay where they are (default t30: moved into 64 subfolders bk00-bk63 at start, renames only; files are found either way); `=undo` moves them back; `THPS_DATA_BUCKETS_SECS=n` caps a start's work (default 60) |
+| `THPS_GL_SAMEBYTES=0` | texture writes of the bytes already there are done anyway (default t31: skipped) |
+| `THPS_GL_PRECISEINV=0` | a texture write reaches the cached pages by 16x16 cells at the next draw (default t31: its exact rectangle) |
+| `THPS_GL_PARTIAL=0` | cached pages a write reaches are freed (default t31: pages drawn lately have the written rows decoded again in place) |
 | `THPS_FILE_DIRECT=0` | Vita: game files read with stdio as before t28 (default: sceIoRead in pieces of 1 MB, an open reads only the header) |
 | `THPS_GL_DECODE_THREADS=n` | Vita: texture cache pages decoded by n threads on cores 1-3 with the game thread (default 3, 0 = the game thread alone) |
 | `THPS_GL_NODISCARD=0` | OpenGL ES (Vita), batched 3D: no separate no-discard, no-blend program for opaque faces with no transparent texel under them |
